title Constel dev-net harness r1 — a named fake dev-net, quarantined by its name, runs the real protocol from genesis
prompt Keep taking the next agent-doable Lindy-first crux; approve own design rounds; double-seat; send each increment; stop at custody gates.
think The fixed 1,024-round road stands complete across all four seasons and no red is open (REDS #72/73/74 all closed). The next agent-doable Lindy-first crux lives in the double-seat expansion, Season D, where the loop just seated the Constel naming law — whose own words name the next rung: the dev-net harness that draws its constellation names from that law. Crux-first: this harness is the decisive move that opens the rest of Season D (Mycelium consensus, Puddle fleet orchestration, every Comlink settlement test all need a fake net to run against inside the jail); high Lindy — a dev-net bench is run for years.
think Fused the crux into one line: a fake dev-net can only be named by a provably-non-@p name (a digit anywhere), and under that name it runs the real settlement protocol from genesis. The name carries the quarantine, not a flag a caller could forget — spin_up refuses UnsafeName BEFORE any genesis opens, so a dev-net cannot exist un-quarantined by construction. name_safe mirrors constel_naming_scan.sh's one digit-check in Rye, so the harness draws from the seated law rather than inventing a parallel rule.
think Composed over the settled modules (settlement.open real genesis + verify) exactly as ship_pilot_identity does — same imports through the pond/apps symlinks (constellation.rye · kumara_tilak.rye · kumara.rye), same demo seeds (0x11/0x22, galaxy 3 under the compass sky), same main(init: std.process.Init) idiom. The fake net is genuine protocol: a forged bind (BadBind) and a non-galaxy number (NotGenesis) each refuse behind the name gate.
obs Landed pond/apps/constel_net.rye (spin_up · name_safe · Constel struct with owned name buffer, bounded max_name_len 32) and tools/constel_net_witness.rish. Selftest GREEN, 5 cases: a law-safe name spins up a real verified demo genesis; every one of the 5 seated draws is law-safe (harness draws from the law); an @p-shaped name (sarlev, no digit) refuses UnsafeName with no genesis opened; a non-galaxy number refuses NotGenesis behind a safe name; empty + overlong names refuse before genesis. The witness also re-runs constel_naming_witness GREEN, so the law stands at the harness's door.
obs tame_style_check bans clean, width-check exit 0, no bare-ordinal prose (GRAD whole-tree seal honored). ≥2 asserts per function, each // invariant. Demo seeds only — no real key, no network, no custody; the maintainer's own Kumara instance stays gate #4, a served constel reaches the serve gate. Two sends this round: the exploration doc (its own signed round, both remotes), then r1 code+witness+this log.
